{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schema\": \"aos-material-review/v1\", \"request_id\": \"qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013-r1\", \"task_id\": \"qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013\", \"owner\": \"codex-01a107a2-e9e4-7670-bc44-1144fa9b27e2\", \"kind\": \"quality\", \"baseline\": {\"head\": \"a283becd94ceabda033b0fcc43e45ba28998fe5e\", \"authority_revision\": \"AOS-001988\", \"files\": {\".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-0.txt\": \"7aeaa84c491cd51cb6848f85a1db330b492fb20d560938d2cd440ea682061ece\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-1.txt\": \"69171adb471083436fb3b0af0e9449b0f422ac5a49aa077a5625077c078ed801\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-2.txt\": \"bbe12fcad820f294d2d7d0386b1973f26e6b1c529426028a13b65083e721bfd5\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-3.txt\": \"10df6b9c8f427111df7f86d60813d8a0b525065b706e8b5d2e0d9733d79f096d\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-4.txt\": \"f57788ab70aff233e1ac9268871c617e4ef19db1dc4c3ccfa7e95c4d4703cdd1\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-5.txt\": \"23a667c4ab1144b4399214307c5a4adce0cfb725c3e5001f620200a6cdd8ddd2\"}}, \"claims\": [\"The added person loader reads persisted profiles through a readonly platform transaction without legacy seed or database writes.\", \"The complete profile cache is published only after successful read and validation; connection or invalid-row failures preserve prior cache.\", \"Managed readonly catalog boot adds strict profile hydration while retaining canonical org/workspace/membership and unchanged legacy and memory branches.\", \"These code and isolated-test findings do not prove actual live display-name restoration or eight runtime workbench acceptance.\"], \"materials\": {\".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-0.txt\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"TWA.12 / 168 — normalize email/phone to canonical membership subject.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport re\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\nfrom aos_api.db import connect_read_only\\nfrom aos_api.logging_facade import get_logger\\n\\nlog = get_logger(\\\"aos-api.person-identity\\\")\\n\\n_EMAIL_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^[^@\\\\s]+@[^@\\\\s]+\\\\.[^@\\\\s]+$\\\")\\n_PHONE_DIGITS = re.compile(r\\\"[^\\\\d+]\\\")\\n\\n# subject -> profile\\n_PERSONS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\\n\\n\\ndef load_profiles_from_db(*, strict: bool = False) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Hydrate existing profiles without legacy seeds or database writes.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global _PERSONS\\n    from aos_api.tenant_catalog import persistence_enabled\\n\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        return 0\\n    try:\\n        with connect_read_only(inherit_scope=False, platform_role=True) as conn:\\n            rows = conn.execute(\\n                \\\"SELECT subject, email, phone, display_name, title \\\"\\n                \\\"FROM twa_person_profile ORDER BY subject\\\"\\n            ).fetchall()\\n        loaded = {}\\n        for row in rows:\\n            subject = row[\\\"subject\\\"]\\n            if not isinstance(subject, str) or not subject.strip():\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"invalid persisted person subject\\\")\\n            loaded[subject] = {\\n                \\\"subject\\\": subject,\\n                \\\"email\\\": row[\\\"email\\\"],\\n                \\\"phone\\\": row[\\\"phone\\\"],\\n                \\\"displayName\\\": row[\\\"display_name\\\"],\\n                \\\"title\\\": row[\\\"title\\\"],\\n            }\\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — compatibility mode retains prior cache\\n        if strict:\\n            raise\\n        log.warning(\\\"person_profile_load_fail\\\", exc_info=True)\\n        return 0\\n    # Publish only after the complete read and validation succeeds.\\n    _PERSONS = loaded\\n    log.info(\\\"person_profile_load count=%s\\\", len(loaded))\\n    return len(loaded)\\n\\n\\ndef reset_person_store() -> None:\\n    _PERSONS.clear()\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.truncate_persons()\\n\\n\\ndef upsert_person_profile(\\n    subject: str,\\n    *,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n    title: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    if not sub:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"subject required\\\")\\n    prev = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {}))\\n    if email:\\n        prev[\\\"email\\\"] = normalize_email(email)\\n    if phone:\\n        prev[\\\"phone\\\"] = normalize_phone(phone)\\n    if display_name:\\n        prev[\\\"displayName\\\"] = display_name.strip()\\n    if title:\\n        prev[\\\"title\\\"] = title.strip()\\n    prev[\\\"subject\\\"] = sub\\n    _PERSONS[sub] = prev\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(prev)\\n    return dict(prev)\\n\\n\\ndef seed_dev_persons() -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bind human profiles to Dev seed subjects (alice / user:dev / bob).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"alice\\\",\\n        email=\\\"alice@acme.example\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613800138000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"艾丽斯\\\",\\n        title=\\\"组织所有者\\\",\\n    )\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"user:dev\\\",\\n        email=\\\"dev@local.aos\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613900139000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"本机开发者\\\",\\n        title=\\\"本机 Bearer 登录账号\\\",\\n    )\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"bob\\\",\\n        email=\\\"bob@acme.example\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613700137000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"鲍勃\\\",\\n        title=\\\"运营查看者\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef normalize_email(raw: str) -> str:\\n    addr = (raw or \\\"\\\").strip().lower()\\n    if not addr or not _EMAIL_RE.match(addr):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid email\\\")\\n    return addr\\n\\n\\ndef normalize_phone(raw: str) -> str:\\n    s = _PHONE_DIGITS.sub(\\\"\\\", (raw or \\\"\\\").strip())\\n    if not s:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid phone\\\")\\n    if s.startswith(\\\"00\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+\\\" + s[2:]\\n    if s.isdigit() and len(s) == 11 and s.startswith(\\\"1\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+86\\\" + s\\n    if s.isdigit() and not s.startswith(\\\"+\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+\\\" + s\\n    if not s.startswith(\\\"+\\\") or len(re.sub(r\\\"\\\\D\\\", \\\"\\\", s)) < 8:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid phone\\\")\\n    return s\\n\\n\\ndef subject_from_email(email: str) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"email:{normalize_email(email)}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef subject_from_phone(phone: str) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"phone:{normalize_phone(phone)}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef resolve_member_identity(\\n    *,\\n    subject: str | None = None,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Prefer email > phone > subject. Returns canonical subject + profile fields.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from aos_api import account_link as alink\\n\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    em = (email or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    ph = (phone or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    # 200m — if contact is linked to an IdP subject, use that subject\\n    linked = None\\n    try:\\n        linked = alink.find_subject_by_contact(\\n            email=em or None,\\n            phone=ph or None,\\n        )\\n    except ValueError:\\n        linked = None\\n    if linked:\\n        existing = _PERSONS.get(linked, {})\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": linked,\\n            \\\"email\\\": normalize_email(em) if em else existing.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": normalize_phone(ph) if ph else existing.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n            or existing.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n            or linked,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"linked\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif em:\\n        canon = subject_from_email(em)\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": canon,\\n            \\\"email\\\": normalize_email(em),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": _PERSONS.get(canon, {}).get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip() or normalize_email(em),\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"email\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif ph:\\n        canon = subject_from_phone(ph)\\n        e164 = normalize_phone(ph)\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": canon,\\n            \\\"email\\\": _PERSONS.get(canon, {}).get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": e164,\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip() or e164,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"phone\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif sub:\\n        existing = _PERSONS.get(sub, {})\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"email\\\": existing.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": existing.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n            or existing.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n            or sub,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"subject\\\",\\n        }\\n    else:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"email, phone, or subject required\\\")\\n\\n    prev = _PERSONS.get(profile[\\\"subject\\\"], {})\\n    merged = {**prev, **{k: v for k, v in profile.items() if v}}\\n    _PERSONS[profile[\\\"subject\\\"]] = merged\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(merged)\\n    log.info(\\n        \\\"person_resolve subject=%s kind=%s\\\",\\n        profile[\\\"subject\\\"],\\n        profile[\\\"kind\\\"],\\n    )\\n    return merged\\n\\n\\ndef get_profile(subject: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    prof = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {}))\\n    if not prof:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"displayLabel\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"email\\\": None,\\n            \\\"phone\\\": None,\\n            \\\"title\\\": None,\\n        }\\n    out = {\\n        \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n        \\\"displayName\\\": prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\") or sub,\\n        \\\"displayLabel\\\": prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"email\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"phone\\\")\\n        or sub,\\n        \\\"email\\\": prof.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n        \\\"phone\\\": prof.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n        \\\"title\\\": prof.get(\\\"title\\\"),\\n    }\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef update_own_profile(\\n    subject: str,\\n    *,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    title: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Update profile for login subject. Does NOT change membership subject key.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    if not sub:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"subject required\\\")\\n    prev = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {\\\"subject\\\": sub}))\\n    if display_name is not None:\\n        prev[\\\"displayName\\\"] = display_name.strip() or sub\\n    if title is not None:\\n        t = title.strip()\\n        if t:\\n            prev[\\\"title\\\"] = t\\n        else:\\n            prev.pop(\\\"title\\\", None)\\n    if email is not None:\\n        if email.strip() == \\\"\\\":\\n            prev.pop(\\\"email\\\", None)\\n        else:\\n            prev[\\\"email\\\"] = normalize_email(email)\\n    if phone is not None:\\n        if phone.strip() == \\\"\\\":\\n            prev.pop(\\\"phone\\\", None)\\n        else:\\n            prev[\\\"phone\\\"] = normalize_phone(phone)\\n    prev[\\\"subject\\\"] = sub\\n    _PERSONS[sub] = prev\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(prev)\\n    log.info(\\\"person_profile_update subject=%s\\\", sub)\\n    return get_profile(sub)\\n\\n\\ndef enrich_member_row(row: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = row.get(\\\"subject\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n    prof = _PERSONS.get(sub, {})\\n    out = dict(row)\\n    if prof.get(\\\"email\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"email\\\"] = prof[\\\"email\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"phone\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"phone\\\"] = prof[\\\"phone\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"title\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"title\\\"] = prof[\\\"title\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"displayName\\\"] = prof[\\\"displayName\\\"]\\n    label = (\\n        prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"email\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"phone\\\")\\n        or sub\\n    )\\n    out[\\\"displayLabel\\\"] = label\\n    return out\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-1.txt\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Boot / schema for Org · Workspace · Membership persistence (164 v1.1).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom aos_api.db import connect, connect_platform\\nfrom aos_api.logging_facade import get_logger\\n\\nlog = get_logger(\\\"aos-api.tenant-catalog\\\")\\n\\n_schema_ready = False\\n\\n# Created by alembic migrations. The runtime login has USAGE but not CREATE on\\n# ``public`` (verified: has_schema_privilege(..., 'public', 'CREATE') = false),\\n# so any DDL attempt fails even with IF NOT EXISTS — PostgreSQL checks the\\n# privilege before it checks object existence. Probe instead of issuing DDL.\\n_CATALOG_TABLES = (\\\"meta_org\\\", \\\"meta_workspace\\\", \\\"meta_membership\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef persistence_enabled() -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return whether the tenant catalog may read/write PostgreSQL.\\n\\n    ``AOS_TWA_STORE=memory`` is the unit-test/in-process boundary and must not\\n    silently mutate the shared ``meta_*`` catalog.  ``auto`` and ``pg`` keep\\n    the existing durable behavior.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    return twa_pg.enabled()\\n\\n\\ndef _catalog_tables_present() -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"True when every catalog table already exists in this database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    try:\\n        with connect_platform() as conn:\\n            row = conn.execute(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n                SELECT count(*) AS n\\n                FROM pg_class\\n                WHERE relkind = 'r' AND relname = ANY(%s)\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\",\\n                (list(_CATALOG_TABLES),),\\n            ).fetchone()\\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — treat probe failure as \\\"not ready\\\"\\n        log.debug(\\\"tenant_catalog_probe_skip\\\", exc_info=True)\\n        return False\\n    return int(row[\\\"n\\\"]) == len(_CATALOG_TABLES)\\n\\n\\ndef ensure_tenant_catalog_schema() -> None:\\n    global _schema_ready\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        return\\n    if _schema_ready:\\n        return\\n    if _catalog_tables_present():\\n        # Normal production path: migrations own the schema, the runtime role\\n        # only reads/writes rows. Short-circuit before any DDL so a privilege\\n        # error can never be mistaken for \\\"persistence unavailable\\\".\\n        _schema_ready = True\\n        return\\n    with connect(inherit_scope=False) as conn:\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_org (\\n              id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n              name TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'standard',\\n              join_policy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'invite_or_apply',\\n              discoverable BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_workspace (\\n              org_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              project_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              name TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              deletable BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,\\n              kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'custom',\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\\n              PRIMARY KEY (org_id, project_id)\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_membership (\\n              org_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              project_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              subject TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              role TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\\n              PRIMARY KEY (org_id, project_id, subject)\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.commit()\\n    _schema_ready = True\\n    log.info(\\\"tenant_catalog_schema_ready\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef boot_tenant_catalogs(*, read_only: bool = False) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load PG → memory only; do **not** auto-seed dev-org.\\n\\n    Non-legacy startup uses read_only=True: require migrated tables, load in\\n    read-only transactions and propagate failures instead of starting with empty\\n    caches that could trigger request-time bootstrap writes.\\n\\n    dev-org / dev-project / 默认人员等测试数据已迁移到 ``aos_api.demo.seed_test_org``。\\n    企业上线后由管理员自建组织；开发/测试显式执行 ``seed_test_org()``。\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        log.info(\\\"tenant_catalog_boot_skipped store=memory\\\")\\n        return\\n    if read_only:\\n        if not _catalog_tables_present():\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"TENANT_CATALOG_SCHEMA_UNAVAILABLE\\\")\\n    else:\\n        ensure_tenant_catalog_schema()\\n    from aos_api import membership as mem\\n    from aos_api import orgs as org_store\\n    from aos_api import workspaces_catalog as ws_cat\\n\\n    if read_only:\\n        org_store.load_orgs_from_db(strict=True)\\n        ws_cat.load_workspaces_from_db(strict=True)\\n        mem.load_memberships_from_db(strict=True)\\n        from aos_api.person_identity import load_profiles_from_db\\n\\n        load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    else:\\n        org_store.load_orgs_from_db()\\n        ws_cat.load_workspaces_from_db()\\n        mem.load_memberships_from_db()\\n    log.info(\\n        \\\"tenant_catalog_booted orgs=%s workspaces=%s members=%s\\\",\\n        org_store.org_count(),\\n        ws_cat.workspace_count(),\\n        mem.membership_count(),\\n    )\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-2.txt\": \"from contextlib import contextmanager\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom aos_api import db, person_identity as person, tenant_catalog\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef profiles(monkeypatch):\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: True)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(person, '_PERSONS', {})\\n    return monkeypatch\\n\\n\\ndef test_persisted_profile_survives_cold_cache_with_native_readonly_connection(profiles):\\n    with db.connect_platform() as conn:\\n        assert conn.info.dbname.startswith('aos_test_')\\n        conn.execute(\\\"INSERT INTO twa_person_profile(subject,display_name,title) VALUES(%s,%s,%s)\\\",\\n                     ('human:cold-profile-test', 'Persisted administrator', 'Administrator'))\\n        conn.commit()\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['displayName'] == 'human:cold-profile-test'\\n    observed = []\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def readonly(**kwargs):\\n        assert kwargs == {'inherit_scope': False, 'platform_role': True}\\n        with db.connect_read_only(**kwargs) as conn:\\n            assert conn.execute('SHOW transaction_read_only').fetchone()['transaction_read_only'] == 'on'\\n            observed.append(True)\\n            yield conn\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', readonly, raising=False)\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True) >= 1\\n    assert observed == [True]\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['displayName'] == 'Persisted administrator'\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['email'] is None\\n    with db.connect_platform() as conn:\\n        assert conn.execute(\\\"SELECT count(*) AS n FROM twa_person_profile WHERE subject=%s\\\", ('human:cold-profile-test',)).fetchone()['n'] == 1\\n\\n\\ndef test_failed_strict_load_preserves_existing_cache(profiles):\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def unavailable(**kwargs):\\n        raise RuntimeError('profile catalog unavailable')\\n        yield\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', unavailable, raising=False)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='profile catalog unavailable'):\\n        person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db() == 0\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n\\n\\ndef test_memory_mode_never_connects_or_replaces_profile(profiles):\\n    profiles.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: False)\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    def forbidden(**kwargs):\\n        raise AssertionError('memory mode must never connect')\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', forbidden, raising=False)\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True) == 0\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n\\n\\ndef test_invalid_row_never_publishes_a_partial_profile_cache(profiles):\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    class Connection:\\n        def execute(self, query):\\n            assert query.startswith('SELECT ') and 'FROM twa_person_profile' in query\\n            return self\\n        def fetchall(self):\\n            return [dict(subject='new', display_name='New', email=None, phone=None, title=None),\\n                    dict(subject='', display_name='Invalid', email=None, phone=None, title=None)]\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def readonly(**kwargs):\\n        yield Connection()\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', readonly)\\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match='invalid persisted person subject'):\\n        person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    assert set(person._PERSONS) == {'preserved'}\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-3.txt\": \"from contextlib import contextmanager\\nimport ast\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom aos_api import membership, orgs, person_identity, tenant_catalog, workspaces_catalog\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef catalog(monkeypatch):\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: True)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', lambda: True)\\n    for module, name in [(orgs, '_ORGS'), (workspaces_catalog, '_WS'), (membership, '_MEMBERS'), (person_identity, '_PERSONS')]:\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(module, name, {})\\n    def forbidden(*args, **kwargs):\\n        raise AssertionError('read-only boot/query must not persist or run DDL')\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'ensure_tenant_catalog_schema', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(orgs, '_persist_org', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspaces_catalog, '_persist_ws', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(membership, '_persist_member', forbidden)\\n    return monkeypatch\\n\\n\\ndef test_readonly_boot_preserves_existing_viewer_and_queries_never_write(catalog):\\n    rows = {\\n        'meta_org': [dict(id='org-org', name='existing', kind='saas', join_policy='invite_only', discoverable=False)],\\n        'meta_workspace': [dict(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', name='existing workspace', deletable=False, kind='custom')],\\n        'meta_membership': [dict(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', subject='existing-user', role='viewer')],\\n        'twa_person_profile': [dict(subject='existing-user', display_name='Existing viewer', email=None, phone=None, title=None)],\\n    }\\n    class Connection:\\n        def execute(self, sql):\\n            assert sql.strip().startswith('SELECT')\\n            self.rows = next(values for table, values in rows.items() if 'FROM '+table in sql)\\n            return self\\n        def fetchall(self):\\n            return self.rows\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def connect(*, inherit_scope, platform_role):\\n        assert inherit_scope is False and platform_role is True\\n        yield Connection()\\n    for module in (orgs, workspaces_catalog, membership, person_identity):\\n        catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_read_only', connect, raising=False)\\n    # Execute the actual non-legacy startup branch, then the actual read routers.\\n    tree = ast.parse((Path(__file__).parents[2] / 'aos_api' / 'main.py').read_text())\\n    body = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.AsyncFunctionDef) and n.name == '_lifespan_body')\\n    branch = next(n for n in body.body if isinstance(n, ast.If) and isinstance(n.test, ast.UnaryOp) and isinstance(n.test.operand, ast.Name) and n.test.operand.id == 'legacy_bootstrap')\\n    exec(compile(ast.Module(body=[branch], type_ignores=[]), '<actual startup branch>', 'exec'), {'legacy_bootstrap': False})\\n    from aos_api.routers.me import me, person\\n    from aos_api.routers.workspaces import list_workspaces\\n    principal = SimpleNamespace(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', subject='existing-user', roles=['viewer'], markings=[], token_kind='test')\\n    assert me(principal)['orgName'] == 'existing'\\n    assert me(principal)['displayName'] == 'Existing viewer'\\n    assert list_workspaces(principal)['items'][0]['name'] == 'existing workspace'\\n    membership.ensure_default_membership('org-org', 'dev-project', 'existing-user')\\n    assert membership.list_members('org-org', 'dev-project')[0]['role'] == 'viewer'\\n    assert orgs.get_org('org-org')['name'] == 'existing'\\n    assert workspaces_catalog.get_workspace('org-org', 'dev-project')['name'] == 'existing workspace'\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_tables_refuses_without_ddl(catalog):\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', lambda: False)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='TENANT_CATALOG_SCHEMA_UNAVAILABLE'):\\n        tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs(read_only=True)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('module,loader', [(orgs, 'load_orgs_from_db'), (workspaces_catalog, 'load_workspaces_from_db'), (membership, 'load_memberships_from_db')])\\ndef test_strict_load_failure_is_not_empty_catalog(catalog, module, loader):\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def unavailable(**kwargs):\\n        raise RuntimeError('catalog connection failed')\\n        yield\\n    catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_platform', unavailable)\\n    catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_read_only', unavailable)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='catalog connection failed'):\\n        getattr(module, loader)(strict=True)\\n    assert getattr(module, loader)() == 0\\n\\n\\ndef test_nonlegacy_lifespan_executes_strict_catalog_boot():\\n    path = Path(__file__).parents[2] / 'aos_api' / 'main.py'\\n    tree = ast.parse(path.read_text())\\n    body = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.AsyncFunctionDef) and n.name == '_lifespan_body')\\n    branch = next((n for n in body.body if isinstance(n, ast.If) and isinstance(n.test, ast.UnaryOp) and isinstance(n.test.operand, ast.Name) and n.test.operand.id == 'legacy_bootstrap'), None)\\n    assert branch is not None\\n    calls = [n for n in ast.walk(branch) if isinstance(n, ast.Call) and isinstance(n.func, ast.Name) and n.func.id == 'boot_tenant_catalogs']\\n    assert any(k.arg == 'read_only' and isinstance(k.value, ast.Constant) and k.value.value is True for c in calls for k in c.keywords)\\n\\n\\ndef test_memory_boot_keeps_existing_cache_and_never_connects(catalog):\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: False)\\n    orgs._ORGS['existing'] = {'id': 'existing', 'name': 'preserved'}\\n    def forbidden():\\n        raise AssertionError('memory mode must not access PG')\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', forbidden)\\n    tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs(read_only=True)\\n    assert orgs._ORGS['existing']['name'] == 'preserved'\\n\\n\\ndef test_legacy_boot_keeps_original_loader_contract(catalog):\\n    calls = []\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'ensure_tenant_catalog_schema', lambda: calls.append('schema'))\\n    for module, loader in [(orgs, 'load_orgs_from_db'), (workspaces_catalog, 'load_workspaces_from_db'), (membership, 'load_memberships_from_db')]:\\n        catalog.setattr(module, loader, lambda: calls.append('load'))\\n    tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs()\\n    assert calls == ['schema', 'load', 'load', 'load']\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-4.txt\": \"# Managed person-profile cold-start correction\\n\\nRules:231,41-TX.3,132-TWC.3, original person/tenant metadata source and managed readonly startup. Current actual original API/Web login works as authenticated UUID in org-org/dev-project; org button displays Qiyuehui company. Original persisted profile display_name datong838 is present, but nonlegacy lifespan only boot_tenant_catalogs meta org/workspace/membership; person cache remains empty and me falls back to UUID.\\n\\nCandidates:1 this safe independent metadata hydration;2 original approved installation runtime-preparation/eight configuration dependencies, requiring current Host/Owner/Source authorization and real storage/tool bindings. Choose1 without opening business runtime or changing DB.\\n\\nFiles: services/aos-api/aos_api/person_identity.py; services/aos-api/aos_api/tenant_catalog.py; services/aos-api/tests/tenant_isolation/test_tenant_catalog_readonly_startup.py; services/aos-api/tests/test_person_profile_cold_start.py. Add original-style load_profiles_from_db strict/read-only loader using connect_read_only(inherit_scope=False,platform_role=True), build rows before atomically replacing person cache, no writes/DDL/seeds. Managed readonly boot calls strict loader after canonical catalogs. Keep legacy bootstrap and memory mode unchanged, do not run whole legacy twa hydration because it would overwrite canonical Qiyuehui name with historical technical org-org. Strict schema/connection failure surfaces; never clear cache into false success. Profiles support existing optional contacts/title without fabricating values.\\n\\nMeaningful RED: actual cold persisted profile after cache clear returns correct displayName, readonly connection guarantees and failed load preserve old cache; actual nonlegacy startup plus me executes original loaders and profile, asserts no DDL/persist path. Adjacent original tenant readonly/memory and TWA12 profile tests, correct isolated lab ownership before pytest, current source freeze/reload and browser profile readback with all650 tables unchanged. Existing local login grant, approved installation, Host/worker/Provider OFF and real data preserved. No fake user/admin, alternate Goal, full eight-page claim or shared-browser credentials inspection.\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-5.txt\": \"{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"MANAGED_READONLY_PERSON_PROFILE_COLDSTART_CODE_GREEN\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": {\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/aos_api/person_identity.py\\\": \\\"7aeaa84c491cd51cb6848f85a1db330b492fb20d560938d2cd440ea682061ece\\\",\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/aos_api/tenant_catalog.py\\\": \\\"69171adb471083436fb3b0af0e9449b0f422ac5a49aa077a5625077c078ed801\\\",\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/tests/tenant_isolation/test_tenant_catalog_readonly_startup.py\\\": \\\"10df6b9c8f427111df7f86d60813d8a0b525065b706e8b5d2e0d9733d79f096d\\\",\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/tests/test_person_profile_cold_start.py\\\": \\\"bbe12fcad820f294d2d7d0386b1973f26e6b1c529426028a13b65083e721bfd5\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"red\\\": {\\n    \\\"failed\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"passed\\\": 7\\n  },\\n  \\\"adjacentGreen\\\": 20,\\n  \\\"finalProfileTargetedGreen\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"nativeColdProfileAndReadonlyObserved\\\": true,\\n  \\\"atomicCacheAndFailurePreservationVerified\\\": true,\\n  \\\"legacyAndMemoryBehaviorPreserved\\\": true,\\n  \\\"currentDatabaseWrites\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"liveApiReloaded\\\": false,\\n  \\\"actualHumanDisplayNameAccepted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"eightWorkbenchesAccepted\\\": false\\n}\\n\"}}"}],"timestamp":1791834659901}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schema\": \"aos-material-review/v1\", \"request_id\": \"qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013-r1\", \"task_id\": \"qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013\", \"owner\": \"codex-01a107a2-e9e4-7670-bc44-1144fa9b27e2\", \"kind\": \"quality\", \"baseline\": {\"head\": \"a283becd94ceabda033b0fcc43e45ba28998fe5e\", \"authority_revision\": \"AOS-001988\", \"files\": {\".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-0.txt\": \"7aeaa84c491cd51cb6848f85a1db330b492fb20d560938d2cd440ea682061ece\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-1.txt\": \"69171adb471083436fb3b0af0e9449b0f422ac5a49aa077a5625077c078ed801\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-2.txt\": \"bbe12fcad820f294d2d7d0386b1973f26e6b1c529426028a13b65083e721bfd5\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-3.txt\": \"10df6b9c8f427111df7f86d60813d8a0b525065b706e8b5d2e0d9733d79f096d\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-4.txt\": \"f57788ab70aff233e1ac9268871c617e4ef19db1dc4c3ccfa7e95c4d4703cdd1\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-5.txt\": \"23a667c4ab1144b4399214307c5a4adce0cfb725c3e5001f620200a6cdd8ddd2\"}}, \"claims\": [\"The added person loader reads persisted profiles through a readonly platform transaction without legacy seed or database writes.\", \"The complete profile cache is published only after successful read and validation; connection or invalid-row failures preserve prior cache.\", \"Managed readonly catalog boot adds strict profile hydration while retaining canonical org/workspace/membership and unchanged legacy and memory branches.\", \"These code and isolated-test findings do not prove actual live display-name restoration or eight runtime workbench acceptance.\"], \"materials\": {\".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-0.txt\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"TWA.12 / 168 — normalize email/phone to canonical membership subject.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport re\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\nfrom aos_api.db import connect_read_only\\nfrom aos_api.logging_facade import get_logger\\n\\nlog = get_logger(\\\"aos-api.person-identity\\\")\\n\\n_EMAIL_RE = re.compile(r\\\"^[^@\\\\s]+@[^@\\\\s]+\\\\.[^@\\\\s]+$\\\")\\n_PHONE_DIGITS = re.compile(r\\\"[^\\\\d+]\\\")\\n\\n# subject -> profile\\n_PERSONS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\\n\\n\\ndef load_profiles_from_db(*, strict: bool = False) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Hydrate existing profiles without legacy seeds or database writes.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global _PERSONS\\n    from aos_api.tenant_catalog import persistence_enabled\\n\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        return 0\\n    try:\\n        with connect_read_only(inherit_scope=False, platform_role=True) as conn:\\n            rows = conn.execute(\\n                \\\"SELECT subject, email, phone, display_name, title \\\"\\n                \\\"FROM twa_person_profile ORDER BY subject\\\"\\n            ).fetchall()\\n        loaded = {}\\n        for row in rows:\\n            subject = row[\\\"subject\\\"]\\n            if not isinstance(subject, str) or not subject.strip():\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"invalid persisted person subject\\\")\\n            loaded[subject] = {\\n                \\\"subject\\\": subject,\\n                \\\"email\\\": row[\\\"email\\\"],\\n                \\\"phone\\\": row[\\\"phone\\\"],\\n                \\\"displayName\\\": row[\\\"display_name\\\"],\\n                \\\"title\\\": row[\\\"title\\\"],\\n            }\\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — compatibility mode retains prior cache\\n        if strict:\\n            raise\\n        log.warning(\\\"person_profile_load_fail\\\", exc_info=True)\\n        return 0\\n    # Publish only after the complete read and validation succeeds.\\n    _PERSONS = loaded\\n    log.info(\\\"person_profile_load count=%s\\\", len(loaded))\\n    return len(loaded)\\n\\n\\ndef reset_person_store() -> None:\\n    _PERSONS.clear()\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.truncate_persons()\\n\\n\\ndef upsert_person_profile(\\n    subject: str,\\n    *,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n    title: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    if not sub:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"subject required\\\")\\n    prev = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {}))\\n    if email:\\n        prev[\\\"email\\\"] = normalize_email(email)\\n    if phone:\\n        prev[\\\"phone\\\"] = normalize_phone(phone)\\n    if display_name:\\n        prev[\\\"displayName\\\"] = display_name.strip()\\n    if title:\\n        prev[\\\"title\\\"] = title.strip()\\n    prev[\\\"subject\\\"] = sub\\n    _PERSONS[sub] = prev\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(prev)\\n    return dict(prev)\\n\\n\\ndef seed_dev_persons() -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bind human profiles to Dev seed subjects (alice / user:dev / bob).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"alice\\\",\\n        email=\\\"alice@acme.example\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613800138000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"艾丽斯\\\",\\n        title=\\\"组织所有者\\\",\\n    )\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"user:dev\\\",\\n        email=\\\"dev@local.aos\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613900139000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"本机开发者\\\",\\n        title=\\\"本机 Bearer 登录账号\\\",\\n    )\\n    upsert_person_profile(\\n        \\\"bob\\\",\\n        email=\\\"bob@acme.example\\\",\\n        phone=\\\"+8613700137000\\\",\\n        display_name=\\\"鲍勃\\\",\\n        title=\\\"运营查看者\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef normalize_email(raw: str) -> str:\\n    addr = (raw or \\\"\\\").strip().lower()\\n    if not addr or not _EMAIL_RE.match(addr):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid email\\\")\\n    return addr\\n\\n\\ndef normalize_phone(raw: str) -> str:\\n    s = _PHONE_DIGITS.sub(\\\"\\\", (raw or \\\"\\\").strip())\\n    if not s:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid phone\\\")\\n    if s.startswith(\\\"00\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+\\\" + s[2:]\\n    if s.isdigit() and len(s) == 11 and s.startswith(\\\"1\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+86\\\" + s\\n    if s.isdigit() and not s.startswith(\\\"+\\\"):\\n        s = \\\"+\\\" + s\\n    if not s.startswith(\\\"+\\\") or len(re.sub(r\\\"\\\\D\\\", \\\"\\\", s)) < 8:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"invalid phone\\\")\\n    return s\\n\\n\\ndef subject_from_email(email: str) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"email:{normalize_email(email)}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef subject_from_phone(phone: str) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"phone:{normalize_phone(phone)}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef resolve_member_identity(\\n    *,\\n    subject: str | None = None,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Prefer email > phone > subject. Returns canonical subject + profile fields.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from aos_api import account_link as alink\\n\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    em = (email or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    ph = (phone or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    # 200m — if contact is linked to an IdP subject, use that subject\\n    linked = None\\n    try:\\n        linked = alink.find_subject_by_contact(\\n            email=em or None,\\n            phone=ph or None,\\n        )\\n    except ValueError:\\n        linked = None\\n    if linked:\\n        existing = _PERSONS.get(linked, {})\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": linked,\\n            \\\"email\\\": normalize_email(em) if em else existing.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": normalize_phone(ph) if ph else existing.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n            or existing.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n            or linked,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"linked\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif em:\\n        canon = subject_from_email(em)\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": canon,\\n            \\\"email\\\": normalize_email(em),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": _PERSONS.get(canon, {}).get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip() or normalize_email(em),\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"email\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif ph:\\n        canon = subject_from_phone(ph)\\n        e164 = normalize_phone(ph)\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": canon,\\n            \\\"email\\\": _PERSONS.get(canon, {}).get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": e164,\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip() or e164,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"phone\\\",\\n        }\\n    elif sub:\\n        existing = _PERSONS.get(sub, {})\\n        profile = {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"email\\\": existing.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n            \\\"phone\\\": existing.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": (display_name or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n            or existing.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n            or sub,\\n            \\\"kind\\\": \\\"subject\\\",\\n        }\\n    else:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"email, phone, or subject required\\\")\\n\\n    prev = _PERSONS.get(profile[\\\"subject\\\"], {})\\n    merged = {**prev, **{k: v for k, v in profile.items() if v}}\\n    _PERSONS[profile[\\\"subject\\\"]] = merged\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(merged)\\n    log.info(\\n        \\\"person_resolve subject=%s kind=%s\\\",\\n        profile[\\\"subject\\\"],\\n        profile[\\\"kind\\\"],\\n    )\\n    return merged\\n\\n\\ndef get_profile(subject: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    prof = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {}))\\n    if not prof:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"displayName\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"displayLabel\\\": sub,\\n            \\\"email\\\": None,\\n            \\\"phone\\\": None,\\n            \\\"title\\\": None,\\n        }\\n    out = {\\n        \\\"subject\\\": sub,\\n        \\\"displayName\\\": prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\") or sub,\\n        \\\"displayLabel\\\": prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"email\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"phone\\\")\\n        or sub,\\n        \\\"email\\\": prof.get(\\\"email\\\"),\\n        \\\"phone\\\": prof.get(\\\"phone\\\"),\\n        \\\"title\\\": prof.get(\\\"title\\\"),\\n    }\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef update_own_profile(\\n    subject: str,\\n    *,\\n    display_name: str | None = None,\\n    email: str | None = None,\\n    phone: str | None = None,\\n    title: str | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Update profile for login subject. Does NOT change membership subject key.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sub = (subject or \\\"\\\").strip()\\n    if not sub:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"subject required\\\")\\n    prev = dict(_PERSONS.get(sub, {\\\"subject\\\": sub}))\\n    if display_name is not None:\\n        prev[\\\"displayName\\\"] = display_name.strip() or sub\\n    if title is not None:\\n        t = title.strip()\\n        if t:\\n            prev[\\\"title\\\"] = t\\n        else:\\n            prev.pop(\\\"title\\\", None)\\n    if email is not None:\\n        if email.strip() == \\\"\\\":\\n            prev.pop(\\\"email\\\", None)\\n        else:\\n            prev[\\\"email\\\"] = normalize_email(email)\\n    if phone is not None:\\n        if phone.strip() == \\\"\\\":\\n            prev.pop(\\\"phone\\\", None)\\n        else:\\n            prev[\\\"phone\\\"] = normalize_phone(phone)\\n    prev[\\\"subject\\\"] = sub\\n    _PERSONS[sub] = prev\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    twa_pg.upsert_person(prev)\\n    log.info(\\\"person_profile_update subject=%s\\\", sub)\\n    return get_profile(sub)\\n\\n\\ndef enrich_member_row(row: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    sub = row.get(\\\"subject\\\") or \\\"\\\"\\n    prof = _PERSONS.get(sub, {})\\n    out = dict(row)\\n    if prof.get(\\\"email\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"email\\\"] = prof[\\\"email\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"phone\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"phone\\\"] = prof[\\\"phone\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"title\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"title\\\"] = prof[\\\"title\\\"]\\n    if prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\"):\\n        out[\\\"displayName\\\"] = prof[\\\"displayName\\\"]\\n    label = (\\n        prof.get(\\\"displayName\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"email\\\")\\n        or prof.get(\\\"phone\\\")\\n        or sub\\n    )\\n    out[\\\"displayLabel\\\"] = label\\n    return out\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-1.txt\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Boot / schema for Org · Workspace · Membership persistence (164 v1.1).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom aos_api.db import connect, connect_platform\\nfrom aos_api.logging_facade import get_logger\\n\\nlog = get_logger(\\\"aos-api.tenant-catalog\\\")\\n\\n_schema_ready = False\\n\\n# Created by alembic migrations. The runtime login has USAGE but not CREATE on\\n# ``public`` (verified: has_schema_privilege(..., 'public', 'CREATE') = false),\\n# so any DDL attempt fails even with IF NOT EXISTS — PostgreSQL checks the\\n# privilege before it checks object existence. Probe instead of issuing DDL.\\n_CATALOG_TABLES = (\\\"meta_org\\\", \\\"meta_workspace\\\", \\\"meta_membership\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef persistence_enabled() -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return whether the tenant catalog may read/write PostgreSQL.\\n\\n    ``AOS_TWA_STORE=memory`` is the unit-test/in-process boundary and must not\\n    silently mutate the shared ``meta_*`` catalog.  ``auto`` and ``pg`` keep\\n    the existing durable behavior.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    from aos_api import twa_pg\\n\\n    return twa_pg.enabled()\\n\\n\\ndef _catalog_tables_present() -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"True when every catalog table already exists in this database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    try:\\n        with connect_platform() as conn:\\n            row = conn.execute(\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n                SELECT count(*) AS n\\n                FROM pg_class\\n                WHERE relkind = 'r' AND relname = ANY(%s)\\n                \\\"\\\"\\\",\\n                (list(_CATALOG_TABLES),),\\n            ).fetchone()\\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — treat probe failure as \\\"not ready\\\"\\n        log.debug(\\\"tenant_catalog_probe_skip\\\", exc_info=True)\\n        return False\\n    return int(row[\\\"n\\\"]) == len(_CATALOG_TABLES)\\n\\n\\ndef ensure_tenant_catalog_schema() -> None:\\n    global _schema_ready\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        return\\n    if _schema_ready:\\n        return\\n    if _catalog_tables_present():\\n        # Normal production path: migrations own the schema, the runtime role\\n        # only reads/writes rows. Short-circuit before any DDL so a privilege\\n        # error can never be mistaken for \\\"persistence unavailable\\\".\\n        _schema_ready = True\\n        return\\n    with connect(inherit_scope=False) as conn:\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_org (\\n              id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n              name TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'standard',\\n              join_policy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'invite_or_apply',\\n              discoverable BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_workspace (\\n              org_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              project_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              name TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              deletable BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,\\n              kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'custom',\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\\n              PRIMARY KEY (org_id, project_id)\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta_membership (\\n              org_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              project_id TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              subject TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              role TEXT NOT NULL,\\n              updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),\\n              PRIMARY KEY (org_id, project_id, subject)\\n            )\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        )\\n        conn.commit()\\n    _schema_ready = True\\n    log.info(\\\"tenant_catalog_schema_ready\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef boot_tenant_catalogs(*, read_only: bool = False) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load PG → memory only; do **not** auto-seed dev-org.\\n\\n    Non-legacy startup uses read_only=True: require migrated tables, load in\\n    read-only transactions and propagate failures instead of starting with empty\\n    caches that could trigger request-time bootstrap writes.\\n\\n    dev-org / dev-project / 默认人员等测试数据已迁移到 ``aos_api.demo.seed_test_org``。\\n    企业上线后由管理员自建组织；开发/测试显式执行 ``seed_test_org()``。\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not persistence_enabled():\\n        log.info(\\\"tenant_catalog_boot_skipped store=memory\\\")\\n        return\\n    if read_only:\\n        if not _catalog_tables_present():\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"TENANT_CATALOG_SCHEMA_UNAVAILABLE\\\")\\n    else:\\n        ensure_tenant_catalog_schema()\\n    from aos_api import membership as mem\\n    from aos_api import orgs as org_store\\n    from aos_api import workspaces_catalog as ws_cat\\n\\n    if read_only:\\n        org_store.load_orgs_from_db(strict=True)\\n        ws_cat.load_workspaces_from_db(strict=True)\\n        mem.load_memberships_from_db(strict=True)\\n        from aos_api.person_identity import load_profiles_from_db\\n\\n        load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    else:\\n        org_store.load_orgs_from_db()\\n        ws_cat.load_workspaces_from_db()\\n        mem.load_memberships_from_db()\\n    log.info(\\n        \\\"tenant_catalog_booted orgs=%s workspaces=%s members=%s\\\",\\n        org_store.org_count(),\\n        ws_cat.workspace_count(),\\n        mem.membership_count(),\\n    )\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-2.txt\": \"from contextlib import contextmanager\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom aos_api import db, person_identity as person, tenant_catalog\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef profiles(monkeypatch):\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: True)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(person, '_PERSONS', {})\\n    return monkeypatch\\n\\n\\ndef test_persisted_profile_survives_cold_cache_with_native_readonly_connection(profiles):\\n    with db.connect_platform() as conn:\\n        assert conn.info.dbname.startswith('aos_test_')\\n        conn.execute(\\\"INSERT INTO twa_person_profile(subject,display_name,title) VALUES(%s,%s,%s)\\\",\\n                     ('human:cold-profile-test', 'Persisted administrator', 'Administrator'))\\n        conn.commit()\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['displayName'] == 'human:cold-profile-test'\\n    observed = []\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def readonly(**kwargs):\\n        assert kwargs == {'inherit_scope': False, 'platform_role': True}\\n        with db.connect_read_only(**kwargs) as conn:\\n            assert conn.execute('SHOW transaction_read_only').fetchone()['transaction_read_only'] == 'on'\\n            observed.append(True)\\n            yield conn\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', readonly, raising=False)\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True) >= 1\\n    assert observed == [True]\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['displayName'] == 'Persisted administrator'\\n    assert person.get_profile('human:cold-profile-test')['email'] is None\\n    with db.connect_platform() as conn:\\n        assert conn.execute(\\\"SELECT count(*) AS n FROM twa_person_profile WHERE subject=%s\\\", ('human:cold-profile-test',)).fetchone()['n'] == 1\\n\\n\\ndef test_failed_strict_load_preserves_existing_cache(profiles):\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def unavailable(**kwargs):\\n        raise RuntimeError('profile catalog unavailable')\\n        yield\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', unavailable, raising=False)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='profile catalog unavailable'):\\n        person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db() == 0\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n\\n\\ndef test_memory_mode_never_connects_or_replaces_profile(profiles):\\n    profiles.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: False)\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    def forbidden(**kwargs):\\n        raise AssertionError('memory mode must never connect')\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', forbidden, raising=False)\\n    assert person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True) == 0\\n    assert person.get_profile('preserved')['displayName'] == 'Existing'\\n\\n\\ndef test_invalid_row_never_publishes_a_partial_profile_cache(profiles):\\n    person._PERSONS['preserved'] = {'subject': 'preserved', 'displayName': 'Existing'}\\n    class Connection:\\n        def execute(self, query):\\n            assert query.startswith('SELECT ') and 'FROM twa_person_profile' in query\\n            return self\\n        def fetchall(self):\\n            return [dict(subject='new', display_name='New', email=None, phone=None, title=None),\\n                    dict(subject='', display_name='Invalid', email=None, phone=None, title=None)]\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def readonly(**kwargs):\\n        yield Connection()\\n    profiles.setattr(person, 'connect_read_only', readonly)\\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match='invalid persisted person subject'):\\n        person.load_profiles_from_db(strict=True)\\n    assert set(person._PERSONS) == {'preserved'}\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-3.txt\": \"from contextlib import contextmanager\\nimport ast\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom aos_api import membership, orgs, person_identity, tenant_catalog, workspaces_catalog\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef catalog(monkeypatch):\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: True)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', lambda: True)\\n    for module, name in [(orgs, '_ORGS'), (workspaces_catalog, '_WS'), (membership, '_MEMBERS'), (person_identity, '_PERSONS')]:\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(module, name, {})\\n    def forbidden(*args, **kwargs):\\n        raise AssertionError('read-only boot/query must not persist or run DDL')\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'ensure_tenant_catalog_schema', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(orgs, '_persist_org', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(workspaces_catalog, '_persist_ws', forbidden)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(membership, '_persist_member', forbidden)\\n    return monkeypatch\\n\\n\\ndef test_readonly_boot_preserves_existing_viewer_and_queries_never_write(catalog):\\n    rows = {\\n        'meta_org': [dict(id='org-org', name='existing', kind='saas', join_policy='invite_only', discoverable=False)],\\n        'meta_workspace': [dict(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', name='existing workspace', deletable=False, kind='custom')],\\n        'meta_membership': [dict(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', subject='existing-user', role='viewer')],\\n        'twa_person_profile': [dict(subject='existing-user', display_name='Existing viewer', email=None, phone=None, title=None)],\\n    }\\n    class Connection:\\n        def execute(self, sql):\\n            assert sql.strip().startswith('SELECT')\\n            self.rows = next(values for table, values in rows.items() if 'FROM '+table in sql)\\n            return self\\n        def fetchall(self):\\n            return self.rows\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def connect(*, inherit_scope, platform_role):\\n        assert inherit_scope is False and platform_role is True\\n        yield Connection()\\n    for module in (orgs, workspaces_catalog, membership, person_identity):\\n        catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_read_only', connect, raising=False)\\n    # Execute the actual non-legacy startup branch, then the actual read routers.\\n    tree = ast.parse((Path(__file__).parents[2] / 'aos_api' / 'main.py').read_text())\\n    body = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.AsyncFunctionDef) and n.name == '_lifespan_body')\\n    branch = next(n for n in body.body if isinstance(n, ast.If) and isinstance(n.test, ast.UnaryOp) and isinstance(n.test.operand, ast.Name) and n.test.operand.id == 'legacy_bootstrap')\\n    exec(compile(ast.Module(body=[branch], type_ignores=[]), '<actual startup branch>', 'exec'), {'legacy_bootstrap': False})\\n    from aos_api.routers.me import me, person\\n    from aos_api.routers.workspaces import list_workspaces\\n    principal = SimpleNamespace(org_id='org-org', project_id='dev-project', subject='existing-user', roles=['viewer'], markings=[], token_kind='test')\\n    assert me(principal)['orgName'] == 'existing'\\n    assert me(principal)['displayName'] == 'Existing viewer'\\n    assert list_workspaces(principal)['items'][0]['name'] == 'existing workspace'\\n    membership.ensure_default_membership('org-org', 'dev-project', 'existing-user')\\n    assert membership.list_members('org-org', 'dev-project')[0]['role'] == 'viewer'\\n    assert orgs.get_org('org-org')['name'] == 'existing'\\n    assert workspaces_catalog.get_workspace('org-org', 'dev-project')['name'] == 'existing workspace'\\n\\n\\ndef test_missing_tables_refuses_without_ddl(catalog):\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', lambda: False)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='TENANT_CATALOG_SCHEMA_UNAVAILABLE'):\\n        tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs(read_only=True)\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('module,loader', [(orgs, 'load_orgs_from_db'), (workspaces_catalog, 'load_workspaces_from_db'), (membership, 'load_memberships_from_db')])\\ndef test_strict_load_failure_is_not_empty_catalog(catalog, module, loader):\\n    @contextmanager\\n    def unavailable(**kwargs):\\n        raise RuntimeError('catalog connection failed')\\n        yield\\n    catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_platform', unavailable)\\n    catalog.setattr(module, 'connect_read_only', unavailable)\\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match='catalog connection failed'):\\n        getattr(module, loader)(strict=True)\\n    assert getattr(module, loader)() == 0\\n\\n\\ndef test_nonlegacy_lifespan_executes_strict_catalog_boot():\\n    path = Path(__file__).parents[2] / 'aos_api' / 'main.py'\\n    tree = ast.parse(path.read_text())\\n    body = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.AsyncFunctionDef) and n.name == '_lifespan_body')\\n    branch = next((n for n in body.body if isinstance(n, ast.If) and isinstance(n.test, ast.UnaryOp) and isinstance(n.test.operand, ast.Name) and n.test.operand.id == 'legacy_bootstrap'), None)\\n    assert branch is not None\\n    calls = [n for n in ast.walk(branch) if isinstance(n, ast.Call) and isinstance(n.func, ast.Name) and n.func.id == 'boot_tenant_catalogs']\\n    assert any(k.arg == 'read_only' and isinstance(k.value, ast.Constant) and k.value.value is True for c in calls for k in c.keywords)\\n\\n\\ndef test_memory_boot_keeps_existing_cache_and_never_connects(catalog):\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'persistence_enabled', lambda: False)\\n    orgs._ORGS['existing'] = {'id': 'existing', 'name': 'preserved'}\\n    def forbidden():\\n        raise AssertionError('memory mode must not access PG')\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, '_catalog_tables_present', forbidden)\\n    tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs(read_only=True)\\n    assert orgs._ORGS['existing']['name'] == 'preserved'\\n\\n\\ndef test_legacy_boot_keeps_original_loader_contract(catalog):\\n    calls = []\\n    catalog.setattr(tenant_catalog, 'ensure_tenant_catalog_schema', lambda: calls.append('schema'))\\n    for module, loader in [(orgs, 'load_orgs_from_db'), (workspaces_catalog, 'load_workspaces_from_db'), (membership, 'load_memberships_from_db')]:\\n        catalog.setattr(module, loader, lambda: calls.append('load'))\\n    tenant_catalog.boot_tenant_catalogs()\\n    assert calls == ['schema', 'load', 'load', 'load']\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-4.txt\": \"# Managed person-profile cold-start correction\\n\\nRules:231,41-TX.3,132-TWC.3, original person/tenant metadata source and managed readonly startup. Current actual original API/Web login works as authenticated UUID in org-org/dev-project; org button displays Qiyuehui company. Original persisted profile display_name datong838 is present, but nonlegacy lifespan only boot_tenant_catalogs meta org/workspace/membership; person cache remains empty and me falls back to UUID.\\n\\nCandidates:1 this safe independent metadata hydration;2 original approved installation runtime-preparation/eight configuration dependencies, requiring current Host/Owner/Source authorization and real storage/tool bindings. Choose1 without opening business runtime or changing DB.\\n\\nFiles: services/aos-api/aos_api/person_identity.py; services/aos-api/aos_api/tenant_catalog.py; services/aos-api/tests/tenant_isolation/test_tenant_catalog_readonly_startup.py; services/aos-api/tests/test_person_profile_cold_start.py. Add original-style load_profiles_from_db strict/read-only loader using connect_read_only(inherit_scope=False,platform_role=True), build rows before atomically replacing person cache, no writes/DDL/seeds. Managed readonly boot calls strict loader after canonical catalogs. Keep legacy bootstrap and memory mode unchanged, do not run whole legacy twa hydration because it would overwrite canonical Qiyuehui name with historical technical org-org. Strict schema/connection failure surfaces; never clear cache into false success. Profiles support existing optional contacts/title without fabricating values.\\n\\nMeaningful RED: actual cold persisted profile after cache clear returns correct displayName, readonly connection guarantees and failed load preserve old cache; actual nonlegacy startup plus me executes original loaders and profile, asserts no DDL/persist path. Adjacent original tenant readonly/memory and TWA12 profile tests, correct isolated lab ownership before pytest, current source freeze/reload and browser profile readback with all650 tables unchanged. Existing local login grant, approved installation, Host/worker/Provider OFF and real data preserved. No fake user/admin, alternate Goal, full eight-page claim or shared-browser credentials inspection.\\n\", \".evidence/qyh-managed-person-profile-coldstart-20261013/review-material-5.txt\": \"{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"MANAGED_READONLY_PERSON_PROFILE_COLDSTART_CODE_GREEN\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": {\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/aos_api/person_identity.py\\\": \\\"7aeaa84c491cd51cb6848f85a1db330b492fb20d560938d2cd440ea682061ece\\\",\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/aos_api/tenant_catalog.py\\\": \\\"69171adb471083436fb3b0af0e9449b0f422ac5a49aa077a5625077c078ed801\\\",\\n    \\\"services/aos-api/tests/tenant_isolation/test_tenant_catalog_readonly_startup.py\\\": \\\"10df6b9c8f427111df7f86d60813d8a0b525065b706e8b5d2e0d9733d79f096d\\\",\\n    \\\